 "notes": "Answers: pro_forma 'Yes' prints 'Foreign-owned U.S. DE' across the top, as the Form 5472 instructions ask of a foreign-owned single-member LLC extending its pro forma Form 1120 (that extension is faxed or mailed to the IRS PIN Unit in Ogden, not the regular Form 7004 address). form_code writes the two digits of the return being extended into the two code boxes (12 for Form 1120, which is also the code for the pro forma 1120 that carries Form 5472). calendar_year is the year's last two digits. country is for an address abroad; 'None' leaves it blank. short_year 'Not a short year' ticks nothing. A 'No' to lines 2 to 4 leaves its box blank. A fiscal year's beginning and ending dates (line 5a) are left for the signer, who writes them only when the tax year isn't the calendar year. The XFA layer is dropped by the filler so the filled boxes show.",
